1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,452
Renewable energy resources are either in constant supply, like the Sun, wind, moving water and Earth's heat,

2
00:00:06,452 --> 00:00:11,423
or can be replaced as fast as we use them, like plants. That makes them sustainable.

3
00:00:12,483 --> 00:00:15,560
Solar energy is free and doesn't pollute when used.

4
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:18,993
Photovoltaic panels turn light directly into electricity.

5
00:00:18,993 --> 00:00:25,445
Solar thermal plants and solar furnaces use mirrors to focus the Sun's heat, boiling water to drive turbines.

6
00:00:26,504 --> 00:00:31,831
Molten salt can store the Sun's heat in insulated tanks, like a battery for solar energy,

7
00:00:31,831 --> 00:00:35,974
so electricity can still be generated after sunset or on a cloudy day.

8
00:00:37,034 --> 00:00:42,893
But solar panels are expensive, sunlight varies and stops at night, and panels need a lot of land.

9
00:00:42,893 --> 00:00:47,096
Some contain lead and cadmium that can leak, the metals must be mined,

10
00:00:47,096 --> 00:00:50,351
and birds can crash into panels they mistake for lakes.

11
00:00:51,410 --> 00:00:55,080
Two cans hold the same amount of water at 20 degrees Celsius.

12
00:00:55,080 --> 00:01:00,111
One is painted matt black; the other is shiny silver. Both stand in bright sunshine.

13
00:01:00,111 --> 00:01:03,603
Predict: which water will warm up faster? Pause and decide.

14
00:01:04,662 --> 00:01:10,700
Watch. After 15 minutes the water in the black can is at 29 degrees, and in the shiny can it is at 23.

15
00:01:11,759 --> 00:01:16,908
After 30 minutes the black can has reached 38 degrees, but the shiny can is only at 26.

16
00:01:17,967 --> 00:01:19,269
Explain what you saw.

17
00:01:19,269 --> 00:01:25,603
The matt black surface absorbs most of the Sun's energy, while the shiny surface reflects much of it away.

18
00:01:25,603 --> 00:01:29,746
That is why solar water heaters on roofs have black pipes and panels.

19
00:01:29,746 --> 00:01:35,546
The energy from the Sun is renewable: it will not run out. Pause and explain it in your own words.

20
00:01:36,606 --> 00:01:40,867
People have used windmills for centuries to pump water and grind grain.

21
00:01:40,867 --> 00:01:47,260
Today, wind turns giant turbine blades connected to generators, converting kinetic energy into electricity.

22
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:50,397
Groups of turbines on land or at sea form wind farms.

23
00:01:51,456 --> 00:01:56,783
Wind energy is clean, releasing nothing harmful into the air. But turbines are expensive,

24
00:01:56,783 --> 00:02:01,695
the wind isn't constant, spinning blades can kill birds, and turbines can be noisy.

25
00:02:02,755 --> 00:02:08,378
Hydropower uses moving water. Water held behind a dam is released through turbines, and tides,

26
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:11,219
waves and ocean currents can turn turbines too.

27
00:02:11,219 --> 00:02:17,433
It's clean, but dams are costly, only work in certain places, and flood large areas, destroying habitats.

28
00:02:18,493 --> 00:02:22,932
Geothermal energy uses heat from hot rock and magma below Earth's surface.

29
00:02:22,932 --> 00:02:27,963
It heats underground water into steam to turn turbines, or warms buildings directly.

30
00:02:27,963 --> 00:02:31,692
In Iceland, magma is close to the surface, so it's easy to use.

31
00:02:32,751 --> 00:02:36,835
Biomass comes from living things, like wood, crops and animal waste.

32
00:02:36,835 --> 00:02:41,156
It can be burnt, turned into biogas, or made into biofuels like ethanol.

33
00:02:41,156 --> 00:02:46,779
Burning it releases carbon dioxide, but replanted crops take it back in through photosynthesis.

34
00:02:47,838 --> 00:02:51,863
Biomass is only renewable if it's replaced as quickly as it's used.

35
00:02:51,863 --> 00:02:58,018
Plants can also replace oil in materials: bioplastics are made from corn starch, seaweed or wood chips.

36
00:02:58,018 --> 00:03:02,694
But some companies exaggerate how green they are, which is called greenwashing.

37
00:03:03,753 --> 00:03:09,258
Now it is your turn to shine! Pause the video after each question and try to answer it first.

38
00:03:10,317 --> 00:03:14,756
Question 1: Why are fossil fuels called non-renewable? Pause the video now.

39
00:03:15,815 --> 00:03:19,959
Answer: They take millions of years to form and can only be used once.

40
00:03:21,018 --> 00:03:24,392
Question 2: What is nuclear fission? Pause the video now.

41
00:03:25,451 --> 00:03:29,416
Answer: Splitting a large nucleus, like uranium, to release energy.

42
00:03:30,476 --> 00:03:34,678
Question 3: Name three renewable energy resources. Pause the video now.

43
00:03:35,737 --> 00:03:39,703
Answer: For example solar, wind, hydropower, geothermal or biomass.

44
00:03:40,762 --> 00:03:45,616
Question 4: Give one environmental drawback of wind turbines. Pause the video now.

45
00:03:46,675 --> 00:03:50,522
Answer: Blades can kill birds, or turbines cause noise pollution.
